We are writing to make you aware of a potential financial matter that may be of interest to you regarding the above-referenced property located in {{ county_name }}.

Based on our review of publicly available county records, it appears that the above property was sold at a tax-defaulted public auction. In certain circumstances, when a property sells for more than the amount owed in taxes, penalties, and fees, the difference — known as "excess proceeds" — may be available to former property owners and other parties with a legal interest.

Under California Revenue & Taxation Code Section 4675, parties of interest may have the right to file a claim for these excess proceeds. There is a time-limited window to file such a claim.

WHAT WE CAN OFFER

Golden State Claimant Advisors assists individuals in understanding the excess proceeds claim process, gathering required documentation, and preparing claims for submission. We are not a law firm and do not provide legal advice.

We invite you to contact us to learn more about whether you may be eligible to file a claim and what documentation may be required.

